cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the connectome data (FlyWire / FAFB, MCNS, BANC, hemibrain, MANC) and the cell-type annotations it builds on."
title: "flybrain: label-free cell typing across fly connectomes from wiring alone"
abstract: >-
  Cell typing of Drosophila connectomes from anonymous wiring, without labels
  in the target. A directed graph neural network that sees only connectivity
  types common cell types within FlyWire (FAFB v783) and, with prior matching
  of type sizes and label-free model selection, transfers to other
  connectomes (male CNS, BANC, hemibrain). For the rarest types, the
  transferred GNN selects candidate neurons and graph matching against the
  reference types them; this was tested under pre-registered protocols on the
  BANC brain and, from MANC, on the nerve cords of BANC and the male CNS.
authors:
  - family-names: Vogt
    given-names: Maximilian
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
repository-code: "https://github.com/Paradoxsmile/flybrain"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - Drosophila
  - FlyWire
  - cell types
  - graph neural networks
  - graph matching
  - domain adaptation
  - pre-registration
